 ## Background
-Gaussian Volume Mask was proposed in the paper "Compact 3D Gaussian Representation for Radiance Field" [S1]. It addresses the high memory and storage costs associated with the large number of Gaussians in 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1]. The method builds on the observation that many Gaussians have negligible volume or transparency and can be safely removed without significant quality loss [S1]. It extends the original 3DGS densification and pruning strategy by introducing a learnable mask that is optimized throughout the training process [S1].
+Gaussian Volume Mask was proposed in the paper "Compact 3D Gaussian Representation for Radiance Field" [S2]. It addresses the high memory and storage costs associated with the large number of Gaussians in 3D Gaussian Splatting [S2]. The method builds on the observation that many Gaussians have negligible volume or transparency and can be safely removed without significant quality loss [S2]. It extends the original 3DGS densification and pruning strategy by introducing a learnable mask that is optimized throughout the training process [S2].
 
